WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.600
Let's get into first principles daily, episode 35 for July 10th, 2026, closing the week with

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.900
one more look at where the next 10 times is hiding. Copper cables costing thousands per kilometer

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.820
gave way to glass strands worth pennies once engineers treated data movement as a purity problem

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:26.280
instead of a wiring problem. Copper wire once set the physical limit on how much information could

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:32.520
move between cities. Electrical resistance and the skin effect forced engineers to add repeaters

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:37.140
every few kilometers and accept data rates that topped out in the low megabits.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:42.980
A different approach asked what would happen if the carrier were light traveling through glass

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:49.260
instead of electrons traveling through metal. The answer required glass so free of impurities

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:56.200
that a pulse could cross tens of kilometers before fading below detection. For most of the 20th century

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:02.740
long distance communication relied on copper pairs or coaxial cable. Designers improved

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:09.440
performance by increasing conductor diameter adding loading coils or installing more frequent amplifiers

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:15.500
yet each step remained inside the same electrical framework. The finished cost of a copper trunk

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:21.800
line therefore reflected the price of refined metal, insulation and the labor of splicing heavy

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:28.020
reels every few hundred meters. Because the physics of electron flow in metal was treated as fixed

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:34.840
incremental gains in bandwidth came at steadily rising expense. Telephone companies and equipment

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:40.360
suppliers accepted these costs as the natural price of moving voice or early data traffic.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:47.080
When demand for video or internet traffic appeared, the same copper plants simply could not scale

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:53.520
without prohibitive numbers of new cables and repeaters. The convention persisted because every prior

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.240
network had been built the same way and because the capital already sunk in copper infrastructure made

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:05.440
alternatives appear risky. Under that approach, the cost per bit stayed high enough that widespread

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:12.600
consumer video or cloud scale computing remained economically out of reach. The skin effect concentrated

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:19.000
current near the conductor surface of higher frequencies so simply raising voltage or frequency produced

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:26.320
rapidly growing losses rather than usable capacity gains. Coaxial designs tried to mitigate this by

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:32.020
surrounding the center conductor with a shield and dielectric but the shield itself added weight,

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:38.800
cost and another set of failure modes at every splice. Loading coils reduced distortion on voice

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.960
circuits yet introduced their own inductive limits once data rates climbed above a few

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:50.120
kilobits per second. Each of these refinements treated the metal path as immutable and therefore

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:56.620
concentrated effort on compensating for its shortcomings. The resulting systems required continuous

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:02.640
power feed to line amplifiers, frequent maintenance access and heavy mechanical support structures,

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:09.400
all of which compounded the installed cost because every incremental improvement still operated inside

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:15.760
the same carrier physics. The industry came to view rising expense per added bit as an unavoidable

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.920
feature of progress rather than a signal that the carrier itself needed re-examination.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:27.360
The decisive shift began by discarding the assumption that the carrier had to be electrons in metal.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.720
Light and glass offered far higher frequency and therefore far higher theoretical bandwidth,

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:41.020
but only if the glass itself did not absorb or scatter the photons. A rough magic wand estimate

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:47.720
starts with the raw material. High purity silica is refined from ordinary sand whose commodity value

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:53.680
sits on the order of a few cents per kilogram. Even after accounting for the small mass inside a

00:03:53.920 --> 00:04:00.840
kilometer of fiber, the material floor lies well below one dollar per kilometer. Early copper cables

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:06.780
by contrast carried finished prices measured in thousands of dollars per kilometer once drawing,

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:13.280
insulation and installation were included. That gap produced an idiot index in the high hundreds

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:19.740
or low thousands. The index is calculated by dividing the finished part price by the raw material

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:25.960
cost inside it. When the finished cable reached thousands of dollars while the metal itself sat at a

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:32.380
small fraction of that amount, the ratio climbed into the hundreds or low thousands. The gap lived

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:37.660
almost entirely in the manufacturing steps required to reach the necessary transparency.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:44.000
The first concrete move was the development of vapor phased deposition processes that could

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:50.700
reduce transition metal impurities to parts per billion. Instead of melting and drawing ordinary glass,

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:57.760
engineers created a preform by reacting silicon tetra chloride and oxygen inside a rotating tube,

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:04.920
depositing layer after layer of ultra pure silica. Each added layer removed another source of

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:11.040
absorption, driving attenuation from hundreds of decibels per kilometer down to fractions of a decibel.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:17.460
That single process change eliminated the need for repeaters every few kilometers and thereby

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:24.500
removed the dominant operating cost of the copper system. Objections that such purity could never

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:30.460
be maintained at scale were met by continuous flow reactors that grew preforms large enough for

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:36.640
hundreds of kilometers of fiber from a single run, keeping impurity levels consistent across the

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:43.540
entire length. A second move addressed the light source itself. Early optical links still used

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:49.360
bulky gas lasers or LEDs whose cost and lifetime kept the overall system expensive.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:55.740
Semiconductor diode lasers, once they reach sufficient reliability and spectral purity,

00:05:56.340 --> 00:06:02.700
replace those sources. Because the lasers could be fabricated on wafers and packaged in volume,

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:08.860
their unit cost fell by orders of magnitude while they're electrical to optical efficiency rows.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:16.380
The lower drive power and smaller size also reduced the power and cooling infrastructure around each terminal.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:22.540
Trade-offs such as wavelength drift with temperature were managed by adding simple thermal

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:29.060
electric stabilizers whose added cost was far smaller than the savings from eliminating gas laser

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:36.600
maintenance. A third move refined the fiber-drawing step preforms that had been painstakingly built by

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:42.400
hand were replaced by larger more uniform preforms produced in continuous chemical reactors.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:49.300
The drawing tower itself was instrumented so that diameter variations stayed inside a few micrometers

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:55.540
preserving the waveguide properties without post processing. Each of these changes attacked a

00:06:55.540 --> 00:07:02.600
different term in the cost stack. The preform purity step attacked attenuation. The laser step

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:09.440
attacked terminal equipment costs. The drawing step attacked labor and yield loss. Together they

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:15.220
moved the finished cost of the transmission medium toward the raw material floor while the remaining

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:22.020
system costs shifted to amplifiers and trenching. The cumulative effect was a sustained decline in cost

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:28.220
per bit of roughly two orders of magnitude per decade for several decades after the first low-loss

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:34.760
fibers appeared. Long haul routes that once required heavy copper or microwave towers could now be

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:41.640
served by hair thin strands whose material content was measured in grams. The idiot index of the

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:48.140
fiber itself fell dramatically once the deposition and drawing processes matured. The index for the

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:54.340
complete installed link remains higher because of permitting, trenching, and the optical amplifiers

00:07:54.340 --> 00:08:01.480
still required every 80 to 100 kilometers. Those amplifiers, splicing crews, and rights of way

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:05.660
constitute the stubborn remainder that has not yet reached the physical floor.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:12.720
Exact current figures vary by route and operator, yet the order of magnitude improvement in delivered

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:19.720
bandwidth per dollar is well documented in public telecommunications records. Dispersion and nonlinear

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:25.640
effects still impose practical limits on how far a single wavelength can travel before regeneration

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:32.600
or compensation is needed. The physical act of burying or suspending cable continues to dominate

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:38.940
project budgets in new corridors. Yet the core transmission medium now operates close enough

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:44.680
to its material floor that further gains come mainly from wavelength multiplexing and improved

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:51.340
amplifier spacing rather than from redesigning the glass itself. Redefining the carrier from

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:57.680
electrons in metal to photons in glass compels every downstream cost to be reexamined against the

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:04.640
new constraint of photon loss rather than resistive heating. The same reexamination appears whenever

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:10.780
an entrenched infrastructure continues to add compensation layers because earlier capital commitments

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:17.400
made the original physical path appear permanent. Tomorrow the show returns with another concrete case

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:23.840
or another domain whose raw material floor sits far below its present price. Which everyday

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:29.500
object still carries an idiot index measured in the hundreds because its designers have not yet

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:35.580
asked what the atoms alone would cost? That's a wrap on today's first principles breakdown.

